### Phase 2: Auth Service HTTP Verification Collection
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@authServiceDirect = http://localhost:8081
@internalKey = your_internal_service_key_for_backend_services_only

### 1. Register a new Student (Server enforces ROLE_STUDENT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Alice Student",
  "email": "alice.student@university.edu",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2. Login as Student (Receives JWT with role ROLE_STUDENT)
# @name studentLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice.student@university.edu",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 3. Get Current User Profile as Student
@studentToken = {{studentLogin.response.body.token}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 4. Admin Login with Seeded Credentials
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@system.local",
  "password": "AdminStrongPassword123!"
}

### 5. Admin Generates Teacher Authorization Key
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}
# @name generateKey
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/teacher-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "teacherEmail": "prof.smith@university.edu"
}

### 6. Admin Lists All Teacher Keys
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/teacher-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7. Teacher Registration with WRONG Key (Should Fail 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register/teacher
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Prof. John Smith",
  "email": "prof.smith@university.edu",
  "password": "TeacherPassword123!",
  "secretKey": "TC-WrongSecretKey123456"
}

### 8. Teacher Registration with CORRECT Key (Replace secretKey from step 5 response)
@teacherSecretKey = {{generateKey.response.body.rawSecretKey}}
# @name teacherRegister
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register/teacher
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Prof. John Smith",
  "email": "prof.smith@university.edu",
  "password": "TeacherPassword123!",
  "secretKey": "{{teacherSecretKey}}"
}

### 9. Teacher Login (Receives JWT with role ROLE_TEACHER)
# @name teacherLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "prof.smith@university.edu",
  "password": "TeacherPassword123!"
}

### 10. Get Current User Profile as Teacher
@teacherToken = {{teacherLogin.response.body.token}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### 11. Internal Service: S2S Get User by ID (Direct to auth-service on :8081 with X-Internal-Token)
@userId = {{studentLogin.response.body.userId}}
GET {{authServiceDirect}}/internal/users/{{userId}}
X-Internal-Token: {{internalKey}}

### 12. Internal Service: Unauthorized S2S Call (Without X-Internal-Token -> Should return 401)
GET {{authServiceDirect}}/internal/users/{{userId}}
